# DMA Tapeout Project Context

This repo is a Tiny Tapeout scatter-gather DMA project in the **planning / architecture** phase (early RTL under `src/rtl/`).

## Before nontrivial work

Read `docs/llm/00-index.md` and the files it lists for the task at hand. Prefer those docs over chat memory.

Human summaries live in `docs/human/` (condensed). Do not duplicate long design prose into human docs unless asked.

## Hard constraints

- Budget: **2 Tiny Tapeout tiles max**; treat ~500 DFFs as a soft ceiling
- Start from scratch; TinyDMA-2C is prior art only, not a code source
- Obsidian notes under `C:\Users\lahnb\Documents\Obsidian Vault\Projects\Tiny Tapeout\` are **read-only**
- Prefer shipping a smaller verified V1 over late feature creep
- When proposing features, state DFF / tile impact
- **Memory scope (D11/D12/D19):** both PSRAM dies are DMA endpoints (incl. cross-device); V1 is bulk memcpy via 11-byte TCDs (`ptr[23]` device, `QUIT` end-of-chain; no ALU/ring/cond-stop); ASIC flash R/W is post-V1; see `docs/llm/10-post-v1-features.md`

## TinyDMA-2C prior art (separate context)

- Canonical dump: `docs/llm/prior-art/tinydma-2c.md`
- Skill: `.cursor/skills/tinydma-prior-art/SKILL.md`
- **If any claim is drawn from that context, say so explicitly** (e.g. "Per TinyDMA-2C prior art...").
- Do not present TinyDMA-2C pins, protocols, or widths as this project's decisions unless the user adopts them and docs are updated.

## Implementation style (when RTL exists)

- SystemVerilog port/instance commas at the beginning of lines
- Synchronous active-low reset only (`rst_n`; assert with `if (~rst_n)`)
- No unsolicited extra markdown docs outside `docs/`
